        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "Fly at almost equal settings on the two gauges, e.g. 80/80, 60/6. Throttle and prop levers are well-matched and can be treated almost as one.",
          "tickable": false,
          "source_confidence": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "At 6,000 feet the 59 per cent setting produces 150hp and fuel consumption of eleven gallons an hour at 205kph (110 knots).",
          "tickable": false,
          "source_confidence": 1.0
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "The M14 radial has a rather irritating harmonic in cruise; both prop and throttle levers vibrate sufficiently to blur their handles.",
          "tickable": false,
          "source_confidence": 1.0
        }
      ]
